17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b9708e75-cf57-54fa-8a86-d6a41661f004" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= -9 \\\\[6pt]\n16x - 10y &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=-9 \\\\ 16x - 10y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $-16x$ term that can cancel with the $16x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=-9 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ 16x - 10y &=18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-16x + 10y &= -18 \\\\\n16x - 10y &= 18 \\\\\n0 &= (-18 + 18) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= -9 \\\\\n5y &= -9 + 8x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-9 + 8x}{5} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{9}{5} + \\frac{8}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(u,-\\frac{9}{5} + \\frac{8}{5}u \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542505 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c60e70b-96f8-5431-90cd-a6ae562c2fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, \\frac{1}{6}x + \\frac{2}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542437} {:answer/id #uuid "0e35757a-2c57-5eb8-9b8e-33ffed7823b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542438} {:answer/id #uuid "1cef499e-0ec5-53e4-97d9-a3772813f69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x + 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542447} {:answer/id #uuid "4320905f-2597-5dbe-b58d-bb716941c26e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542463} {:answer/id #uuid "49b76269-cc41-593b-a5e2-31e2fd0a943a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, -4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e35757a-2c57-5eb8-9b8e-33ffed7823b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x, 6x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542438} :answer-field/id #uuid "10860ce5-13d5-5537-a83d-c826703c2441" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef3faa80-f6ae-5cf6-8c47-c5a225be4ccd" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - y &= 4 \\\\[6pt]\n-24x + 4y &= -16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - y &=4 \\\\ -24x + 4y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $24x$ term that can cancel with the $-24x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x - y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ -24x + 4y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n24x - 4y &= 16 \\\\\n-24x + 4y &= -16 \\\\\n0 &= (16 - 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - y &= 4 \\\\\n-y &= 4 - 6x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 - 6x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= -4 + 6x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(x,-4 + 6x \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cac595a2-a76f-5528-90a3-5b43bb6b6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}t + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542496} {:answer/id #uuid "df428421-e8d1-4b41-a517-4bec76a6280f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10-7t}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac595a2-a76f-5528-90a3-5b43bb6b6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}t + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542496} :answer-field/id #uuid "0052794e-29d0-5a14-847c-4f8656980f5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2d5e6d3-70ba-56f0-872c-ec4406eeabb5" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 2y &= 10 \\\\[6pt]\n21x + 6y &= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $t$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(t,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 2y &=10 \\\\ 21x + 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-3$, then we will get a $-21x$ term that can cancel with the $21x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 2y &=10 && \\mid \\cdot (-3) \\\\ 21x + 6y &=30\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-21x - 6y &= -30 \\\\\n21x + 6y &= 30 \\\\\n0 &= (-30 + 30) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 2y &= 10 \\\\\n2y &= 10 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{10 - 7x}{2} \\\\\ny &= 5 - \\frac{7}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $t=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(t,5 - \\frac{7}{2}t \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542509 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e93e99b-7e76-59cd-a8bf-9d5a1e879a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e99b-7e76-59cd-a8bf-9d5a1e879a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542457} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f52dab6-f84a-51c1-bb5e-7609d7d43d80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fd33d3a8-634b-5300-83fe-512c3febb665" :question/problem "Describe the points that lie on the intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x - y &= -4 \\\\[6pt]\n12x + 4y &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress your answer in terms of $t$ only.\n\nThe intersection points are\n\n$(t,$ {{field-1}} $),$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number." :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=-4 \\\\ 12x + 4y &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $4$, then we will get a $-12x$ term that can cancel with the $12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x - y &=-4 && \\mid \\cdot (4) \\\\ 12x + 4y &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - 4y &= -16 \\\\\n12x + 4y &= 16 \\\\\n0 &= (-16 + 16) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x - y &= -4 \\\\\n-y &= -4 + 3x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-4 + 3x}{-1} \\\\\ny &= 4 - 3x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $t=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(t,4 - 3t \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50351666-c691-510f-863c-168c61f9980b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a System With Infinitely Many Intersection Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d56e4e-14df-5e76-8811-2258751260f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{7}{5}u - \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542450} {:answer/id #uuid "2b767e80-1eaf-555b-9465-6842cf1181fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{7}{5}u + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542455} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd62e8-0db4-5e13-9558-c017d95ac564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542478} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ea97ea-40ff-582c-b6e3-88f89d97fe8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, \\frac{7}{5}u + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542489} {:answer/id #uuid "c600e11f-1d2c-53ce-a422-159dac0d2e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{5}{7}u + \\frac{4}{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b767e80-1eaf-555b-9465-6842cf1181fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u, -\\frac{7}{5}u + \\frac{4}{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542455} :answer-field/id #uuid "986fd8e2-7152-5f37-bea8-d024be1e25a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fec9f06c-a4db-563f-96a3-164f1364ae78" :question/problem "Find all points of intersection of the following lines:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 5y &= 4 \\\\[6pt]\n-14x - 10y &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points of intersection of the lines correspond to the solutions of the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 5y &=4 \\\\ -14x - 10y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using elimination. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2$, then we will get a $14x$ term that can cancel with the $-14x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x + 5y &=4 && \\mid \\cdot (2) \\\\ -14x - 10y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhen we add the two equations, it turns out that both variables cancel, and we obtain a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n14x + 10y &= 8 \\\\\n-14x - 10y &= -8 \\\\\n0 &= (8 - 8) \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause we obtained a true statement, we conclude that there are infinitely many solutions to the system. Therefore, the lines have infinitely many intersection points.\n\nWe want to find an expression that represents every solution to the system. Any value of $x$ can be chosen, and we can find the corresponding $y$-coordinate for each $x$-coordinate by solving one of the lines for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7x + 5y &= 4 \\\\\n5y &= 4 - 7x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4 - 7x}{5} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{7}{5}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=x$ be the free coordinate.\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are\n\n$$\n\\left(u,\\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{7}{5}u \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is any number."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "866eae0c-01b3-50bf-b526-86a0c6cac6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561230} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa7f187-7fdf-5a83-ab02-69b55dfb828f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561244} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c3ac96-f810-55fd-8221-e27eafaa255a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "866eae0c-01b3-50bf-b526-86a0c6cac6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561230} :answer-field/id #uuid "8500c6f6-dcab-5691-9d28-5480f89255f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a462c5e-dc46-5cbd-908d-8873a5836bec" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& x + 6 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -3x + 3y &{}={}& 18\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x + 6 \\\\ -3x + 3y &= 18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x + 6\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x + 6\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 3y &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3\\left(x + 6\\right) &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3x + 18 &= 18 \\\\\n18 &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75689f6e-65af-5364-b427-d0d53ea942af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561221} {:answer/id #uuid "79766299-4422-5446-8123-6c952ce516d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561225} {:answer/id #uuid "9eff61d3-41d1-56c6-bd82-959956a2ca75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79766299-4422-5446-8123-6c952ce516d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561225} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec6e71b-2b03-5a5a-9cc6-7eb21d9e2203" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561198}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c389456-1e7f-570a-b81d-ee3996221d09" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x - 2y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -5x + 2y &{}={}& 1\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 2y &=-1 \\\\ -5x + 2y &= 1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 2y &=-1 \\\\\n-2y &= -5x - 1 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-5x - 1}{-2} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + 2y &= 1 \\\\\n-5x + 2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}\\right) &= 1 \\\\\n-5x + 5x + 1 &= 1 \\\\\n1 &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9164734a-796f-5af8-ac94-62a22713d23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561234} {:answer/id #uuid "c60ae584-a9c5-5da2-b67b-9cea1d5ceb12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561246} {:answer/id #uuid "f5850239-8333-5a95-b556-84d53e0aa3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9164734a-796f-5af8-ac94-62a22713d23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561234} :answer-field/id #uuid "8afb3dd7-ffd1-50e9-b1b9-598ad7c3ec84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5dcff32d-252d-58bc-9fa9-cb87cd485a01" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 2x - 3y &{}={}& 0 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 6x - 9y &{}={}& 0\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x - 3y &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 9y &= 0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x - 3y &= 0 \\\\\n-3y &= -2x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-2x}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}x\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x - 9y &= 0 \\\\\n6x - 9\\left(\\frac{2}{3}x\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n6x - 6x &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13da69cb-99ca-554d-8d6d-4260e2aaf8e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561195} {:answer/id #uuid "4417ae70-0890-5813-a5ad-6509930c237e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561206} {:answer/id #uuid "73ba1cde-65b2-5df1-8173-f771c3abe4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73ba1cde-65b2-5df1-8173-f771c3abe4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561220} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b90caf-daee-5b7f-adfd-50fdc0c131c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6542765a-dbf6-5f4b-aedd-6339210b9996" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -5x + y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 10x - 2y &{}={}& 2\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x + y &=-1 \\\\ 10x - 2y &= 2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= 5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x - 2y &= 2 \\\\\n10x - 2\\left(5x - 1\\right) &= 2 \\\\\n10x - 10x + 2 &= 2 \\\\\n2 &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28deb832-44b2-579c-bb80-e65dc4c0107e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561199} {:answer/id #uuid "6f64462a-0a21-5bfe-90c2-09bf574953ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561219} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f350c-25be-5a95-b053-4cbb5ed6e773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb4f350c-25be-5a95-b053-4cbb5ed6e773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561258} :answer-field/id #uuid "087a9931-aed8-58f6-9406-32b8d1499065" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76b29f4c-d2f7-5be9-99e6-f351f6d667d5" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& -5x - 5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 25x + 5y &{}={}& -20\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= -5x - 5 \\\\ 25x + 5y &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = -5x - 5\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25x + 5y &=-20 \\\\\n25x + 5\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -20 \\\\\n25x - 25x - 25 &= -20 \\\\\n-25 &= -20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9537567-1850-5466-995f-5f2a3e4745df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561243} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40c9bc-94bd-5b2a-ac25-2906284d6dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561251} {:answer/id #uuid "cdeed473-c033-56b5-80e0-c80a74ce7f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdeed473-c033-56b5-80e0-c80a74ce7f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561252} :answer-field/id #uuid "47b67ab5-2541-51b1-b6af-87cd3ee8f675" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "787cf7fe-f2f7-5df0-b36f-e78b6273a4b5" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -2x - 3y &{}={}& -4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 12x + 20y &{}={}& 6\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x - 3y &=-4 \\\\ 12x + 20y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 3y &=-4 \\\\\n-3y &= 2x - 4 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{2x - 4}{-3} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n12x + 20y &= 6 \\\\\n12x + 20\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}x + \\frac{4}{3}\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n12x - \\frac{40}{3}x + \\frac{80}{3} &= 6 \\\\\n-\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{80}{3} &= 6 \\\\\n-\\frac{4}{3}x &= - \\frac{62}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805cb854-3cef-5a9d-b52f-6cb5f1a05d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561228} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fd6325-a5dc-5571-807f-0a19cfc212a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561241} {:answer/id #uuid "f61301bd-60c9-56c5-bccb-3ea8e307b4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "805cb854-3cef-5a9d-b52f-6cb5f1a05d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561228} :answer-field/id #uuid "c843a425-7cc2-5a78-8427-4b2970f00770" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96e99e9b-5b2e-55b0-8814-cc28b8bf6bc8" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -x - y &{}={}& 4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -12x - 3y &{}={}& -12\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x - y &= 4 \\\\ -12x - 3y &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x - y &= 4 \\\\\n-y &= x + 4 \\\\\ny &= -x - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-x - 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x - 3y &=-12 \\\\\n-12x - 3\\left(-x - 4\\right) &= -12 \\\\\n-12x + 3x + 12 &= -12 \\\\\n-9x + 12 &= -12 \\\\\n-9x &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561204} {:answer/id #uuid "ce74c59e-9e7a-5fcf-9bfa-74ca29a5dc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561253} {:answer/id #uuid "eeaec689-8e5c-5fbe-a829-38566863fd86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561204} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90c2268-eb7e-5503-ad73-e1ac5a2b2e15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a01d9c5-2885-5132-9235-1d9478baed14" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& -x - 4 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -9x - 3y &{}={}& 15\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= -x - 4 \\\\ -9x - 3y &= 15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = -x - 4\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-x - 4\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-9x - 3y &= 15 \\\\\n-9x - 3\\left(-x - 4\\right) &= 15 \\\\\n-9x + 3x + 12 &= 15 \\\\\n-6x + 12 &= 15 \\\\\n-6x &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64762017-ef57-574d-99d7-a9be2892815d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561217} {:answer/id #uuid "8903af01-7bdb-59b7-bfc2-56796727445a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561231} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec78b20-d253-53dd-af36-f3b3e2a99e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64762017-ef57-574d-99d7-a9be2892815d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561217} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c7459c3-7647-57df-ac62-0f53b2bd604d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4be2362-89eb-587e-82aa-d9d4f04eb125" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -5x - y &{}={}& 5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -20x - 4y &{}={}& -8\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x - y &= 5 \\\\ -20x - 4y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x - y &= 5 \\\\\n-y &= 5x + 5 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-20x - 4y &=-8 \\\\\n-20x - 4\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -8 \\\\\n-20x + 20x + 20 &= -8 \\\\\n20 &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "303e264e-f7bb-58e1-8f43-28746c565777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561201} {:answer/id #uuid "f84d8eb6-0a3f-5c54-b516-d5072df2722e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561263} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1ddb6a-6d38-5bf0-ac22-13dff12c39f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84d8eb6-0a3f-5c54-b516-d5072df2722e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561263} :answer-field/id #uuid "016fa648-d368-50d4-ab14-df62c0c4ad93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c74e2f77-c144-59ff-a39d-154078a44e94" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& 4x + 2 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -8x + 2y &{}={}& 6\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= 4x + 2 \\\\ -8x + 2y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = 4x + 2\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 2\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 8x + 4 &= 6 \\\\\n4 &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da3fcc3-fa0d-5f01-ba15-7551732faeaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561210} {:answer/id #uuid "52d1d98a-2227-583b-995d-2d9f0f210a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561211} {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e62ba3e0-8699-5115-910d-02ee319aed05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561256} :answer-field/id #uuid "43673130-deba-5b98-8ce2-b4ee4ed0101a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7e53da6-3b28-54ab-be32-bc2afa7301df" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x + y &{}={}& -1 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -12x + 3y &{}={}& 3\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x + y &=-1 \\\\ -12x + 3y &= 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= -5x - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-5x - 1\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &= 3 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(-5x - 1\\right) &= 3 \\\\\n-12x - 15x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x - 3 &= 3 \\\\\n-27x &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient of $x$ is nonzero, so this equation determines exactly one value of $x$. The first equation then determines exactly one value of $y$. Therefore, the system has one solution.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at one point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf58711-5f7d-5d0c-9c8b-5e45dbfc55fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561200} {:answer/id #uuid "57e75c5c-9d7e-5fbb-9e68-fd683aeb2452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561212} {:answer/id #uuid "ea88b994-5abc-51ab-a610-96e8bfe4ffaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf58711-5f7d-5d0c-9c8b-5e45dbfc55fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561200} :answer-field/id #uuid "af3666b2-e413-595c-a093-783fa1dc8bf4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c878eb46-3c57-53bc-9b71-6029289efddf" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & y &{}={}& x \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & -5x + 5y &{}={}& 0\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ -5x + 5y &= 0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x + 5y &= 0 \\\\\n-5x + 5\\left(x\\right) &= 0 \\\\\n-5x + 5x &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f19502-4a84-510e-96d9-21e50d95ed63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561202} {:answer/id #uuid "5d633272-a745-52f8-8022-869b2818e9f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561215} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d8f10b-db63-5f68-bb23-678f2810b48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d633272-a745-52f8-8022-869b2818e9f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561215} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4562de-6958-5910-a9b5-816e85d031d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f855e10a-f1b4-5356-9c10-ccedf77e81d7" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & -5x - 2y &{}={}& -5 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 20x + 8y &{}={}& 21\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x - 2y &=-5 \\\\ 20x + 8y &= 21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5x - 2y &=-5 \\\\\n-2y &= 5x - 5 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5x - 5}{-2} \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x + 8y &= 21 \\\\\n20x + 8\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}x + \\frac{5}{2}\\right) &= 21 \\\\\n20x - 20x + 20 &= 21 \\\\\n20 &= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e321ee9-c5ef-59e7-a720-449c297502e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561197} {:answer/id #uuid "96ad7a29-d44e-5997-8a2d-3dd126d93384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561235} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d98a33-6b71-5fc5-8f2b-3c8643f0ca6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e321ee9-c5ef-59e7-a720-449c297502e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561197} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fe7ee01-e7b5-51f5-a15c-7bbfebd4775e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe1a8df0-eeb5-5653-bde4-9ae932e3abc3" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{alignedat}{2}\nl_{1}:\\quad & 5x - 3y &{}={}& 2 \\\\[6pt]\nl_{2}:\\quad & 20x - 12y &{}={}& 7\n\\end{alignedat}\n$$\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x - 3y &= 2 \\\\ 20x - 12y &= 7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - 3y &= 2 \\\\\n-3y &= -5x + 2 \\\\\ny &= \\frac{-5x + 2}{-3} \\\\\ny &= \\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n20x - 12y &= 7 \\\\\n20x - 12\\left(\\frac{5}{3}x - \\frac{2}{3}\\right) &= 7 \\\\\n20x - 20x + 8 &= 7 \\\\\n8 &= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}]}
